course: dictionary
lesson: 12095
title: Cocky: confident or rude?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for «cocky», and the context tells you which one fits. Read the sentence around the word first, then choose the meaning that makes sense.
explain: «Ben kicked two goals and started bragging, too cocky for his own good.» Bragging and too cocky for his own good show that cocky means too sure of yourself in an annoying, rude way. Ask yourself: would this person be fun to be around? If not, that is a clue.
explain: «The cocky farmer counted his sheep at dawn.» Here the words sheep and farmer are the clues. In Australia, cocky can mean a small farmer, as in «a cow cocky». Try the meaning in the sentence: a cocky farmer makes sense, so this is the right meaning.
fact: Cocky is an informal word, so you will mostly find it in stories, sport and everyday talk, not in formal writing.
fact: Cocky means too confident and sure of yourself in an annoying or rude way.
fact: Coaches warn teams not to get cocky, because a team that thinks it has already won can lose.
fact: In Australia, «cocky» is also a friendly name for a cockatoo, the noisy crested parrot.
fact: In Australia, a cocky can also be a small farmer, as in «a cow cocky».
exercise: «Ben kicked two goals and started bragging, too cocky for his own good.» What does cocky mean here? | *Too sure of himself in an annoying way | Covered in mud after the game | Very quiet and shy | Hungry for lunch
exercise: «The cocky farmer counted his sheep at dawn.» Which Australian meaning fits this sentence? | A football boot | A teacher who gives lots of homework | A cloud that brings rain | *A small farmer
exercise: Coaches warn teams not to get cocky. What does the coach mean? | *Do not think you have already won and become too sure of yourself | Do not eat before a game | Do not run very fast | Do not wear your sports kit
test: «Tom was so cocky after the spelling test that he stopped revising.» What does cocky mean? | *Too confident and rude | A kind of bird | Sleepy and slow | Quiet and nervous
test: In Australia, which of these can cocky mean? | A cloud | *A cockatoo, the noisy crested parrot | A grey, wet day | A cricket ball
exam: «Sam's cocky grin said he had already won, though the race had barely started.» What does cocky show about Sam? | He is shy and quiet | *He is too sure of himself in an annoying way | He is a cockatoo | He is feeling ill
